{"nodes": [{"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "label": "Phase 3 Week 4 Decision Log", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One row per decision that would be expensive to re-litigate, with client decisions marked and a reversed-or-superseded table at the end."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d1_transfer_with_folds_fixed", "label": "D1: Transfer, With the Folds Fixed First", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Leave-one-out over four datasets holds out a population, not a disease, and the two strongest folds are the ones with the most influenza leakage; spending seeds on the wrong fold structure buys nothing."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d2_meta_learning_required", "label": "D2: Meta-Learning Is Required, Not Optional", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lets the project answer whether meta-learning beats a linear probe with a number instead of an assertion."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d3_reporting_standards", "label": "D3: Reporting Standards Effective Immediately", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dispersion on every number, no averaging across datasets, comparison reference on the table, and within noise instead of a direction below the floor."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d4_ebola_audit_figures", "label": "D4: Ebola Audit Figures Settled", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Weekly, N=61, T=52, 41% observed, 146 edges and 21 cross-border; support of 27 cells across 9 districts, adaptation pairs h3=16/h5=6/h10=0/h15=0 with the left pad. Two corrections owed the client: the 27-example floor came from Ebola's own support, and h10/h15 are zero-shot rather than unmeasurable."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d5_transfer_reference_and_dispersion", "label": "D5: Transfer-Table Reference and Dispersion", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "train/lodo.py::_report compared LODO to seed 42's own single run while the docs quoted 5-seed means, and seed 42 is an unusually bad single-disease seed, so a seed-matched reference flattered LODO. The formula was correct, the reference was not; both references are now reported with a paired origin bootstrap as the verdict."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d6_heatgnn_epoch_budget", "label": "D6: HeatGNN Epoch Budget Stays at the Paper's 1500", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An earlier 150-epoch run was the deviation, not the standard; cutting epochs would mean diverging from the paper while claiming a match, so speed must come from parallelism instead."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d7_heatgnn_nan_self_loops", "label": "D7: HeatGNN NaN Fixed with Self-Loops on the Staged Graph Only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "getLaplaceMat never folds in the identity and the block that would is commented out, so an isolated node is scaled by ~1e12 rather than erroring; the forward survives and the backward overflows. Japan and us-states each carry two degree-0 nodes and us-regions carries none, which is why only us-regions trained."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d7a_epignn_islands", "label": "D7a: EpiGNN Islands Documented, Not Rerun", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EpiGNN's getLaplaceMat is byte-identical and equally lacks the identity but survives because it has no SIR loss to amplify it; dropping islands shifts node_mean in opposite directions on the two panels, so it is idiosyncrasy not bias. The evidence does not show what EpiGNN would score with self-loops."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d8_csv_skip_trap", "label": "D8: The CSV Skip Trap", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "HeatGNN's trainer exits immediately when the results CSV holds a matching row, while the runner decides work from prediction npz files, so a row without an npz blocks that run forever."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d9_heatgnn_runtime_model", "label": "D9: HeatGNN Runtime Model and Launch Config", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cost tracks training windows, not nodes: japan has 4.7x the nodes of us-regions and runs 2x faster. Not thread-bound, so parallelism is near-linear, and per-run cost must not be projected as s/epoch times 1500 because runs early-stop near 440 epochs."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d10_reproduction_failure_log", "label": "D10: Reproduction Failure Log Scope", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Section A for repos that could not be reproduced and Section B for comparisons that could not be made like-with-like, with each usable baseline validated against its source paper before entering the comparison table."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d11_independent_audit", "label": "D11: Independent Audit of Steps 1 and 2, Both Green", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Audited against artifacts on disk rather than against claims: the run plan was re-derived without trusting remaining(), and all 16 RMSE cells were re-derived from raw JSON without importing analysis.py. Left open: results/lodo JSONs were produced by a version of train/lodo.py that was never committed, so the transfer table's evidentiary base has zero version provenance."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d12_transfer_negative", "label": "D12: Cross-Disease Transfer Is Negative", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Under the corrected disease-level fold, 12 of 16 RMSE cells are significantly negative, 4 within noise and 0 positive; the three largest earlier gains were influenza panels with influenza still in training, and holding the transfer number fixed while varying only the reference reproduces all three client arithmetic complaints to the decimal. The paper's central claim as previously framed is not supported by the project's own corrected experiment."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d13_anil_decision", "label": "D13: ANIL, and the Schedule Answer Is No for the Full Scope", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scope is deliberately not decided here: options go to the client without a recommendation. Three corrections on record, including that the adapter is an exact affine read-out on frozen features and is 1,428 params rather than 388. The self-raised objection is that with two dev diseases, leave-one-disease-out leaves one meta-train disease, so ANIL would be trained on the non-problem."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d14_checkpointing_and_quantiles", "label": "D14: No Further Trunk Run Without Checkpointing and Quantile Archiving", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Zero .pt files existed outside baselines, so every LDO result rested on a trunk that no longer exists and the freeze-the-trunk protocol had nothing to freeze; every scoring path also took the median index and discarded four of five quantiles at source, leaving the calibrated-uncertainty claim with no evidence behind it. Both are cheap now and unrecoverable later."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d15_capacity_probe_control_arm", "label": "D15: Capacity Probe Runs with an In-Domain Control Arm", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Run alone the probe cannot separate a genuine transfer bottleneck from an adapter that was undersized all along and helps everywhere; the control costs no second trunk run and is what makes the result interpretable. The verdict is derived mechanically in code so the call is not a matter of taste."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d16_ebola_support_length", "label": "D16: Ebola Support Length, 12 Weeks Primary and 20 Weeks Secondary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both arms frozen and hashed before either is scored; query counts are identical under both arms so they differ only in labelled adaptation data, which is what makes them comparable. The Phase-2 ebola.npz build is superseded for scoring and the C8 guards were hardened to a prefix match as part of this."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d17_trunk_early_stop", "label": "D17: The Trunk Early Stop Was Real and Cost Nothing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All 15 LDO3 trunks burned exactly 12,000 steps after their best checkpoint, so the cosine schedule scaled to 91,000 steps was a no-op and no trunk could be called converged. A patience-999 rerun found the best value at step 7,000 and never improved, and the scored records are bit-identical, so the verdict does not move; the fix ships anyway because the mismatch will bite a longer-training configuration."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d18_ceiling_early_stop", "label": "D18: The Single-Disease Ceiling Early-Stops Too, 25 of 25", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every transfer number is a ratio against the ceiling, so if only the transfer arm stopped early the deficit would be partly self-inflicted. The attack is removed, but the bias direction runs against transfer: if the ceiling sits below its own optimum the reported deficit understates the true gap. The arms stop on different clocks and the behaviour varies by dataset, so this is not an equal handicap."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_decisions_d19_adapter_capacity_five_seeds", "label": "D19: Adapter Capacity at Five Seeds", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seed-paired deltas against each seed's own affine control: 7 of 36 cross-disease cells clear zero, all at h15, and the in-domain control gains nothing in 12, so the effect is transfer-specific. The caveat that must travel with it is that h15 is exactly where the frozen Ebola primary arm has zero adaptation pairs, and changing the surface now would void the pre-registration."}], "edges": [{"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d1_transfer_with_folds_fixed", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d2_meta_learning_required", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d3_reporting_standards", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d4_ebola_audit_figures", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d5_transfer_reference_and_dispersion", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d6_heatgnn_epoch_budget", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d7_heatgnn_nan_self_loops", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d8_csv_skip_trap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d9_heatgnn_runtime_model", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d10_reproduction_failure_log", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d11_independent_audit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d12_transfer_negative", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d13_anil_decision", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d14_checkpointing_and_quantiles", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d15_capacity_probe_control_arm", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d16_ebola_support_length", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d17_trunk_early_stop", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_decisions_decision_log", "target": "progress_decisions_decisions_d18_ceiling_early_stop", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"s